// `unsafe` marks a function BODY (C#'s meaning). A TYPE has no body, so there is nothing in it to be
// unsafe — and a blanket type-level marker would be the opposite of the greppable-at-the-declaration
// guarantee the seam exists for. Mark the members that touch raw memory instead.
type unsafe value V { public int32 x; }

fn int32 main() { return 0; }
